 :root-cause
 "The shared public consistency descriptor validated the two required token fields but did not reject additional fields. The formal public-input model classified malformed descriptors as rejected, and the documented strict boundary promised unknown-field rejection, so production accepted an input outside the modeled language."
 :fix
 "Require token consistency descriptors to contain exactly two fields, :consistency/mode and :zed/token, using cardinality and membership checks that avoid allocating a key set. Retain a cross-runtime shared regression and an explicit Dafny lemma that malformed consistency input is rejected."
 :closing-evidence
 ["ConsistencyDecision.MalformedConsistencyCannotBeAccepted"
  "eacl.consistency-test/public-consistency-descriptors-reject-unknown-fields-test"]}
